  "note": "Relief is an analytic approximation (two low gravel hills divided by the Walbrook, the Fleet valley to the west, a low marshy south bank) at true vertical scale. It is not derived from a survey or borehole model. Corrected against the 2026 LIDAR comparison (research/lidar.md): Tower Hill reduced to 1 m (no separate crest; it is the end of the Cornhill spur) and the Walbrook valley filled to no more than half its depth by 1600 (it is still about 3.5 m deep today). The City's absolute height has not been lowered: that finding is unverified (docs/CORRECTIONS.md).",
